# Defense in depth: the Dockerfile's runtime stage only COPYs named paths
# (app, alembic, alembic.ini, pyproject.toml), so none of this should ever
# reach the runtime image. This file protects that stage if it's ever changed
# to a broader `COPY . .` and keeps the build context small either way.
#
# tests/ is intentionally NOT excluded: the Dockerfile's `test` stage needs
# it, and the runtime stage never inherits from `test`, so it still never
# ships to production images.
.venv/
.venv_review/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
.env
.git/
